WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-How are you?

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm good, I'm good.
How are you?

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.003 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm well.

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot has changed since
the last time you were here.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are a very recognizabl
person now,

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
even more so than I think
the last time you were here.

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:11.745
And I feel like as someone o
the Intelligence Committee

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:12.579 line:92%
when you're this recognizable,

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:17.751
it kind of means at its core
that something's gone wrong.

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:18.518 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.586 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yes, it can. It can.

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you find that
you're recognized more?

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yes.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:26.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
In fact, I had a rather
unusual experience

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.660 size:84% position:42% line:92%
on my way here tonight.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was on the phone with
one of the major airlines,

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
trying to get back
into my account,

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I couldn't remembe
the password.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.268 line:92%
So I finally get through.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're on
the Intelligence Committee

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just want to remind you that
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:40.807 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-It is a little scary.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:41.441 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, okay.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:43.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, the password was so
secret that not even I could -

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure, sure, sure, right.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:46.913 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-So, I'm on the phone.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:50.050 size:84% position:42%
I finally get through
all the voicemail hell.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.252 line:92%
And I get this disembodied voice

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
walking me through the login
screens, whatever.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:57.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm entering
a new security question.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the question is, "What i
your first dog's name?"

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:02.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I enter the dog's name
but it's too short.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:03.063 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It won't accept it.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:06.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I say, "Won't accept
my dog's name."

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the voice says,
"Try 'impeach.'"

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.938 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I said, "What?"

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.006 line:92%
And he says, "Try 'impeach.'

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:15.408 size:81% position:41%
And I said, "I thought
that's what you said."

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I was trying to be
very professional,

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:19.079 size:78% position:39% line:92%
but I couldn't help."

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:22.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "I'm not going to us
that as the dog's name."

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:23.550 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yes.
-Yeah.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:27.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
So even your voice on the phon
with a major airline,

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.255 line:92%
they know who you are now.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.123 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-They apparently do.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They apparently know
who you are.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think one of the things,
obviously --

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:37.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Latin term
we're all familiar with no

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is quid pro quo.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
We even had, you know, durin
some of the testimony,

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
Gordon Sondland
basically laid it out.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.270 line:92%
This is a Trump appointee.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.573
He said,
"Yes, there was a quid pro quo."

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
And yet, a lot of
the Republicans,

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
most of the Republicans
in the committee,

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
still continue to say
there was no quid pro quo,

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:55.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it is clear as day,
as some would say, there is,

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
it is just as clear to the
there isn't.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this a -- Do you think they
at their core believe this

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:04.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
or is this just a gaslightin
maneuver to let their --

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
let their base,
let the President,

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:09.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
know that they have
their backs in this?

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:09.929 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mostly the latter.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think they really
believe this.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we had exactly
that phenomenon

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.367 line:92%
where we had Sondland testify.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.337
He quite clearly said, "Yo
know, most people want to reduce

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.171 line:92%
this to a simple question.

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:21.274
Well, if you do, the answer is
yes, there was a quid pro quo.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:21.975 line:92%
-Interesting to know that

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
I believe it was
in his opening statement.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was something
that he just offered up.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:25.645 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, yes.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
And nonetheless, Republica
members walked out of

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:32.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
that very hearing saying,
"See, he said no quid pro quo.

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:34.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you listen to that
and you think,

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:37.157
"Okay, were you in the same room
that I was in?

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:38.525 line:92%
Because he very clearly said

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:40.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
'That's exactly
what happened here,

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:43.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not only that,
everyone was in the loop.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:43.963 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And what's more,

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
these were the orders
from the President on down.'

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:51.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
Rudy Giuliani, acting
as his agent, was implementing

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:51.905 size:84% position:42% line:92%
essentially this scheme

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
to condition
the White House meeting.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, later,
$400 million in military aid

00:02:56.109 --> 00:03:01.915
to help the President coerce
Ukraine into basically cheatin

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.983 line:92%
for him in the next election

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's rare to have
a case this strong,

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
this unequivocal,
this overwhelming.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:12.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the astonishing thing abou
it is, normally,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
a complex white-collar crime
case like this,

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:18.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's what this is
analogous to,

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.499 size:88% position:44% line:92%
is very document-driven.

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:20.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
But here,
because the White House said

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:25.238
"You get to see no documents,"
we were able to make the cas

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:28.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
with these career public
servants who did their duty,

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:33.846
who came and testified, suffered
the insults and the attacks,

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:36.249
and because of their patriotism,
we know the truth.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:39.385
And the truth is, the Presiden
of the United States tried t

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:44.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
shake down an ally to help him
cheat in the next election

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So many of these
public servants

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
either served under
both presidents

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:52.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
or were appointees of
a Republican administration.

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:53.700 line:92%
Were you surprised as it went on

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
how quickly they were attacked
for being --

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:59.339
"Never Trumpers" was certainly
the term that was used the most.

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.908
Were you surprised that your
colleagues across the aisl

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
were so quick to attack them
for that?

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:06.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I have
the usual sensation we hav

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.983
in the era of Trump, which is,
you're shocked on the one hand

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're not surprised
on the other.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:13.386
-Yeah, that's about where I feel
every night, yeah, yeah.

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You described it well.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:19.726
-So, you know, here you ha
people like Bill Taylor, who

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:22.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
as his testimony revealed,

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:23.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
graduated top of his class
at West Point.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:27.767
He chooses to go to Vietna
during the height of the war

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.002 line:92%
And I loved when he was asked,

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:31.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he's so self-effacing,
you know.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:34.607
"You got some distinctions
while you served in combat."

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
He says,
"Well, one I'm most proud of

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the combat
infantryman's badge.

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:40.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I also got
a Bronze Star, but, you know

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.547 line:92%
the one I really care about --

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:45.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a guy who is basically
downplaying a Bronze Star.

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:46.085 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this is a guy
they're attacking.

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:50.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
Colonel Vindman
got a Purple Heart.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.491 size:81% position:41% line:92%
They're attacking him.

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:52.959 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Ambassador Yovanovitch

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
had dangerous posts
around the world.

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:57.163 size:81% position:41% line:92%
They're attacking her.

00:04:57.163 --> 00:05:01.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is nothing
beyond their willingness

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.103 size:75% position:38%
to debase themselves
for this President.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:06.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
I keep making the point,

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
what are you going to tell you
grandkids when they ask yo

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:13.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
what you did while
this awful man was in office

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.315 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to stand up to him?

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:17.317 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-He doesn't like you.

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:17.850 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:18.751 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I get that impression.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know if you know that
yeah.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a lot of
the Judiciary Committee,

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:26.959
a lot of the Republicans there
they actually felt that you --

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.261 line:92%
you had a right to be there,

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:31.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you had a right
to answer questions.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
we've referenced the fact

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.167 line:92%
that they have terrible props.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.102 size:78% position:39%
But this is a milk --
a poster board of you

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:38.371
on the side of a milk,
because you were missing.

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:41.474
Now, of course, you weren'
missing. You just were not -

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:43.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was no reason for yo
to be there.

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:47.413
And yet, they frame it as though
you're sort of hiding, you know,

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:48.281 line:92%
somewhere in Congress becaus

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:49.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're too afraid to go
in front of this.

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:54.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has this been strange to watch
them use you as a prop,

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:57.957
being a colleague of theirs even
though of a different party?

00:05:57.957 --> 00:05:58.758 line:92%
-Well, I mean, the reason is

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:00.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
because this is
what Trump wanted.

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:01.194 line:92%
So Trump is tweeting out,

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:02.829 size:88% position:44%
"He should be a witness,
he should be a witness."

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:04.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they will do
whatever the President asks.

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:07.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of my colleagues said,
"We're going to get you

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
a T-shirt that says,
'I'm right here'

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:12.138
that you can wear on the House
floor and just point to it."

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:15.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you know, my favorite sign
frankly, was one

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:18.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
a couple of days
earlier that said,

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:20.813
"It's been zero days since
Adam Schiff followed the rules,"

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:23.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
which means that I was
constantly following the rules

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:27.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.155 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:34.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Okay, finally
an accurate sign."

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:35.795 line:92%
But my staff member said,

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:37.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Did you see the signs
whatever today?"

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:39.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
And actually, I never paid
attention to the signs.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I just tried to keep
my focus on the witnesses.

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:42.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That means the signs
aren't working.

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:45.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
The whole reason you make sign
is for people to see them.

